1. Replace the CPU-only package with the official GPU-enabled build (bundles ROCm + Vulkan runners + matching HIP runtime):
  sudo pacman -Rns ollama                 # remove CPU-only Arch package first (conflicts on /usr/bin/ollama)
  curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh


2. Pin the dGPU + set the backend. Edit the service env:
  sudo systemctl edit ollama
```
[Service]
Environment="OLLAMA_LLM_LIBRARY=rocm"          # use ROCm; swap to "vulkan" as fallback
Environment="HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0"            # renderD128 = 9070 XT
Environment="HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=12.0.1"  # RDNA 4 = gfx1201; only if log shows "unsupported GPU"
```
  sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart ollama


3. Get the model. It's not in the Ollama registry. Two options:
  # (a) Pull GGUF straight from HuggingFace (Ollama 0.4+ hf.co/ namespace)
  ollama pull hf.co/<HF_USER>/Hermes-3-Llama-3.1-8B-lorablated-GGUF:Q4_K_M
  
  # (b) If you already downloaded the .gguf — import via Modelfile (robust, repo-agnostic)
  printf 'FROM ./Hermes-3-Llama-3.1-8B-lorablated-Q4_K_M.gguf\n' > /tmp/M
  ollama create hermes3-lorablated -f /tmp/M


4. Run + verify GPU offload:
  ollama run <model_name>
  # in another terminal:
  ollama ps                                    # PROCESSOR column should read "100% GPU"
  journalctl -u ollama -b | grep -iE "rocm|vulkan|gfx|gpu"   # confirms backend loaded on 9070 XT
